# Scoped to packaging/android/shell/ only -- the repo root .gitignore
# belongs to upstream ForgeHub and this project does not touch it (see
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-forgehub-android-design.md, "Living in
# a fork"). Everything under packaging/android/ is ours, so a local
# .gitignore here is the correct and sufficient fix.

# Gradle's own local state: build caches, lock files, wrapper download
# cache. None of this is portable between machines and all of it is
# reproducible from the committed Gradle config -- it is exactly the kind
# of noise the controller called out (13 of 18 untracked files here before
# this commit were .gradle/ cache internals).
.gradle/

# Build outputs: compiled classes, the APK itself, test reports. Rebuilt
# from source every time; never has a reason to be committed.
build/
*/build/

# Written by Android Studio / the SDK on first sync, points at this
# machine's absolute SDK path -- meaningless (and wrong) on any other
# machine or CI runner.
local.properties

# IDE project state.
.idea/
*.iml

# Controller ruling 4 backstop: the signing keystore must never enter the
# working tree at all (it lives outside the repo, path from an env var --
# see make-release-keystore.sh and app/build.gradle.kts's signingConfigs).
# These patterns exist only in case one is ever created inside this
# directory by mistake; the real control is "don't put one here".
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
